<title>HUNGARY: Hungary one-month bill yield falls to 22.01 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary one-month bill yield falls to 22.01 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of one-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 22.01 percent, down from 22.07 percent at an auction one week ago, the Government Debt Management Centre said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow, and on  HTBM.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received	1,693.62 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 1,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    22.01 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     98.3396 pct</p>
</text>
